  "question": {
    "text": "A bucket full of water weighs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, it is pulled from a well <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> deep. There is a small hole in the bucket through which water leaks at a constant rate. If it is observed that for every metre the bucket loses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.2</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;mass of water, then the total work done in pulling the bucket up from the well is [<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]",
